  "solution": {
    "text": "When benzaldehyde is heated with aqueous ethanolic NaCN or $\\mathrm{KCN},$ it dimerises to form an $\\alpha$ -hydroxy ketone called benzoin, and this reaction is formed as benzoin condensation. It involves self condensation of an aromatic aldehyde in the presence of $\\mathrm{CN}^{-}$ as catalyst.\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2013_che_a10.png\">",
